  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nA novel spectral optimization strategy is proposed to minimize the maximum overlap integral between a step function and its shifted complement. Current methods rely on local search, which often gets trapped in suboptimal regions. We use a quasi-periodic spectral reconstruction combined with iterative thresholding that leverages global phase information. The approach is based on representing candidate solutions in the frequency domain and applying a gradient flow that minimizes the maximum overlap integral. This method avoids numerical instability by working in the spectral space and benefits from global optimization techniques. The primary advantage is the ability to escape local optima effectively.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nVariables: h \u2208 [0,1]^n_points such that sum(h) = n_points/2\nObjective: C5 = max_{k \u2208 Z\\\\{0}} \u222b_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\nEquivalent Formulation: C5 = max_k [ np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full') * dx ] where dx = 2/n_points\n\nImplementation:\n- Frequency Domain: Represent h as a sum of exponential functions\n- Spectral Mapping: Convert problem to frequency domain\n- Iterative Thresholding: Apply soft-thresholding in spectral space\n- Constraint Handling: Maintain sum requirement via dual formulation\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\nInitialize N_medium = 80, N_large = 120\nTime budget distribution: 70% for medium, 30% for large\nFunction generation:\n- Generate f_\u03b8 in F_N via exponential basis\n- Project onto [0,1] with mass constraint\n- Initialize dual variable penalty parameter \u03b2 = 0.1\nAt each iteration:\n1. Forward map: Convert \u03b8 to spectral domain \u03a3\n2. Dual update: Minimize max_{k} |\u03a3_k| with soft-thresholding\n3. Gradient projection: \u03b2\u0303 \u2190 \u03b2 * \u03b3 (\u03b3 = 0.95)\n4. Consistency check: Enforce sum(f_\u03b8) = N/2\n\n4. Search Choices and Useful Variations\n- Frequency resolution: Use N_medium = 80, N_large = 120\n- Thresholding parameter \u03b2 \u2208 [0.05, 0.2]\n- Phase initialization: Random principal phase shift\n- Global vs local search: 50% spectral basis, 50% random trials\n- Local refinement: Three-phase approach\n\n5. Numerical Robustness and Memory Use\n- Memory: O(N_medium + N_large) per evaluation\n- Repair mechanism: Iterative reweighting ensures constraints\n- Convergence: Projection onto simplex ensures boundedness\n- Fall-back heuristic: Projected gradient method if divergence occurs\n\n6. Runtime Safeguards and Return Contract\n- Model evaluation: np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full') * dx\n- Violation repair: Softmax scaling for sum enforcement\n- Convergence detection: Monotonic improvement measured over 10 trials\n- Computation tracking: Count iterations based on spectral basis updates",
